      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nRegister RopeKVCacheFusionPass patterns per distinct attention geometry under _USE_LAYERNAME and convert qkv.split ValueError mismatches into RuntimeError during pattern re-tracing so speculative-decoding drafter graphs with different attention dimensions do not crash torch.compile.\n\nFixes #64679\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes torch._inductor.exc.InductorError (ValueError on qkv.split) when fuse_rope_kvcache runs on a draft_model or EAGLE speculative-decoding drafter whose per-rank QKV width differs from the target model's.\n- Registers fusion patterns for every distinct (num_heads, num_kv_heads, head_size, head_size_v) attention geometry present in static_forward_context.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\npytest tests/compile/passes/test_rope_kvcache_fusion.py -k test_rope_kvcache_fusion_multi_geometry_and_mismatched_qkv_width -v\n```\n\n## Details\n\nWhen _USE_LAYERNAME is enabled, RopeKVCacheFusionPass.__init__ previously registered patterns from only the first attention layer and broke out of the loop. When a drafter or hybrid layer had a different (num_heads, num_kv_heads, head_size, head_size_v) tuple, the structural matcher still matched the drafter's subgraph and Inductor's check_fn re-traced pattern(qkv, ...) with the drafter's qkv tensor. Because qkv.split([q_size, k_size, v_size], dim=-1) raises ValueError on a width mismatch whereas Inductor's check_fn only catches RuntimeError, compilation failed instead of rejecting the candidate match. Deduplicating by attention geometry and translating ValueError to RuntimeError in fwd_and_view_to_reshape allows non-matching patterns to return False cleanly while still fusing all registered geometries.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's /pr-checklist skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
